1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:05,785
In this lesson, you'll learn the three
ways to organise information in Kyntlo:

2
00:00:05,785 --> 00:00:08,359
tags, custom fields and custom values.

3
00:00:08,359 --> 00:00:13,711
Get these right, and your filters,
automations and messages all become far more

4
00:00:13,711 --> 00:00:14,321
powerful.

5
00:00:15,177 --> 00:00:16,761
Here's the short version.

6
00:00:16,761 --> 00:00:20,626
Tags are simple labels that put
people into groups, like vip.

7
00:00:20,626 --> 00:00:25,378
Custom fields store a detail about one
contact, like their last visit date.

8
00:00:25,378 --> 00:00:30,257
And custom values store a detail about
your business, like your booking link,

9
00:00:30,257 --> 00:00:31,905
that you reuse everywhere.

10
00:00:32,826 --> 00:00:34,111
Let's start with tags.

11
00:00:34,111 --> 00:00:35,747
Here's Emma Clarke's record.

12
00:00:35,747 --> 00:00:38,376
Her tags sit on the
left: whitening, and vip.

13
00:00:39,226 --> 00:00:41,293
Click Add tag and start typing.

14
00:00:41,293 --> 00:00:45,828
Kyntlo suggests tags you already
use, so reuse one whenever you can.

15
00:00:45,828 --> 00:00:48,696
If you really need a
new tag, click Create.

16
00:00:49,548 --> 00:00:51,937
Tags are the glue of your automations.

17
00:00:51,937 --> 00:00:54,892
A workflow can start the
moment a tag is added,

18
00:00:54,892 --> 00:00:58,664
like sending a thank-you when
someone is tagged review left.

19
00:00:58,664 --> 00:01:03,002
And in your contact list, you can
filter everyone by tag in a second.

20
00:01:03,852 --> 00:01:06,176
Now scroll down to Additional info.

21
00:01:06,176 --> 00:01:07,769
These are custom fields.

22
00:01:07,769 --> 00:01:13,080
They hold the details that standard fields
don't cover, like treatment interest,

23
00:01:13,080 --> 00:01:15,603
last visit date, or preferred dentist.

24
00:01:15,603 --> 00:01:20,648
Unlike a tag, a field holds a value
that can be different for every contact.

25
00:01:21,498 --> 00:01:24,752
You update them like any
other field, then click Save.

26
00:01:24,752 --> 00:01:28,729
Because they're real fields, you
can filter by them, sort by them,

27
00:01:28,729 --> 00:01:31,802
and even show them as
columns in your contact list.

28
00:01:32,652 --> 00:01:36,668
You create new custom fields in
Settings, under Custom Fields.

29
00:01:36,668 --> 00:01:40,360
Pick a field type, like text,
date, dropdown or checkbox,

30
00:01:40,360 --> 00:01:42,821
and group related fields into folders.

31
00:01:42,821 --> 00:01:45,476
Your forms can fill in custom fields too,

32
00:01:45,476 --> 00:01:49,168
so the details people type in
land right on their record.

33
00:01:49,168 --> 00:01:52,213
We'll walk through Settings
in module fourteen.

34
00:01:53,063 --> 00:01:54,742
Custom values are different.

35
00:01:54,742 --> 00:01:57,560
They belong to your
business, not to a contact.

36
00:01:57,560 --> 00:02:02,056
Think of your booking link, your phone
number, or this month's offer price.

37
00:02:02,056 --> 00:02:05,174
You set them once, in
Settings, under Custom Values.

38
00:02:06,026 --> 00:02:08,296
Here's where it all comes together.

39
00:02:08,296 --> 00:02:12,381
In the message box, click Custom
values to insert placeholders.

40
00:02:12,381 --> 00:02:15,299
Contact fields fill in
each person's details,

41
00:02:15,299 --> 00:02:18,412
and custom values fill
in your business details.

42
00:02:19,885 --> 00:02:24,291
When you send it, Kyntlo swaps each
placeholder for the real value.

43
00:02:24,291 --> 00:02:27,382
Emma sees her own name,
the price and the link.

44
00:02:27,382 --> 00:02:30,933
And if the price changes,
you update one custom value,

45
00:02:30,933 --> 00:02:33,760
and every message that
uses it updates too.

46
00:02:34,611 --> 00:02:35,713
Here's a pro tip.

47
00:02:35,713 --> 00:02:38,822
Agree on a naming style
for tags with your team,

48
00:02:38,822 --> 00:02:43,811
like lowercase words joined with hyphens,
and write down what each tag means.

49
00:02:43,811 --> 00:02:48,476
A tidy tag list keeps your filters
and automations reliable as you grow.

50
00:02:49,385 --> 00:02:50,816
Your data is organised!

51
00:02:50,816 --> 00:02:55,482
In the next lesson, we'll put it to
work with smart lists and bulk actions,

52
00:02:55,482 --> 00:02:58,966
so you can tag, message and
export whole groups at once.

53
00:02:58,966 --> 00:02:59,837
See you there.
